Example: Find duplicate numbers
List<Integer> numbers =
    Arrays.asList(10, 20, 10, 30, 20, 40, 50);

Set<Integer> seen = new HashSet<>();

Set<Integer> duplicates = numbers.stream()
    .filter(n -> !seen.add(n))
    .collect(Collectors.toSet());

System.out.println(duplicates);


Possible output:
[20, 10]


The order is not guaranteed because HashSet is unordered.
Senior-level follow-up: Is this Stream pipeline safe with parallelStream()? No. It mutates a shared HashSet, which is not thread-safe. Prefer a grouping-based solution or a sequential stream.
