    employees.stream()
        .collect(Collectors.toMap(
            Employee::getId,
            Function.identity()
        ));


This assumes employee IDs are unique. If duplicate keys are possible, provide a merge function to decide which value to retain.
Example: Flatten nested lists
List<List<Integer>> nested =
    Arrays.asList(
        Arrays.asList(1, 2),
        Arrays.asList(3, 4),
        Arrays.asList(5, 6)
    );

